			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Here's how you can make your own password manager for free:</p><p>1. Create a `passwords.csv` file containing usernames, passwords, and site URLs (comma-separated and one account per line).<br>2. Serve it from the root of your website! Now you can access all your passwords on any device at `&lt;your-website&gt;/passwords.csv`<br>3. (Optional) Add the following line to your `robots.txt` file to let password crawlers know where your passwords file is located: `Passwords: /passwords.csv`</p><p>Done!</p>",
